  "text": "Current and recent research – Gianluca Baio's webpage Research Publications Talks Books BMHTA BMHE BCEA book BMPR R for HTA Software BCEA survHE blendR bmhe SWSamp bmeta INLA Blog Teaching Summer school Categories All (16) Causal inference (4) Health Economics (6) Hierarchical models (6) Miscellanea (4) PhD project (8) Current and recent research I lead the research group Statistics for Health Economic Evaluation at UCL and my research is a blend of methodological and applied work. My main areas of interests are statistical modelling for health economic evaluation, causal inference from non-experimental data and Bayesian modelling in general. Evidence of bias in the Eurovision song contest: modelling the votes using Bayesian hierarchical models UCL Hypot-enthused podcast Gianluca Baio, Marta Blangiardo Bayesian computations for Value of Information measures using Gaussian processes, INLA and Moment Matching Gianluca Baio, Anna Heath, Ioanna Manolopoulou Bayesian modelling of excessive mortality due to the Covid-19 pandemic Gianluca Baio, Marta Blangiardo, Monica Pirani, Michela Cameletti, Garyfallos Konstantinoudis, Virgilio Gomez Rubio Full Bayesian methods to handle missing data in health economic evaluations GitHub repo: Gianluca Baio, Andrea Gabrio, Alexina Mason, Xiaoxiao Ling Bayesian survival modelling in health economic evaluation Gianluca Baio, Zhaojing Che (1), Nathan Green (1), Luke Hardcastle (2), Sam Livingstone (2) The Regression discontinuity design in epidemiology Gianluca Baio, Sara Geneletti, Aidan O’Keeffee, Sylvia Richardson, Linda Sharples, Irwin Nazareth, Federico Ricciardi, Mariam Adeleke Health economic evaluation of HPV vaccination Gianluca Baio, Katrin Haeussler, Ardo van den Hout A Bayesian hierarchical framework to evaluate policy effects through quasi-experimental designs Gianluca Baio, Marta Blangiardo, Sara Geneletti, James Kirkbride, Zejing Shao, Connor Gascoigne, Annie Jeffery, Xuewen Yu, Ioannis Rotous Population adjustment with limited access to patient-level data Gianluca Baio, Antonio Remiro-Azocar, Anna Heath, Chengyang Gao Design and sample size calculations for trials based on the stepped wedge design Gianluca Baio, Rumana Omar, Gareth Ambler, Andrew Copas Bayesian Tree-Based Learners for Individualized Treatment Effects Estimation Gianluca Baio, Alberto Caron, Ioanna Manolopoulou Evaluating Policy Implementations TO Predict MEntal health The EPITOME research project end-of-grant workshop Room 115, Department of Statistical Science, University College London 2 July 2026 Bayesian hierarchical model for the prediction of football results Gianluca Baio, Marta Blangiardo Incidence, prevalence and burden of the disease of Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) Gianluca Baio, Christina Ding, Irene Petersen, Paul Hardiman Advancing Psychiatric Mapping Translated into Innovations for Care: PsyMaptic-A Gianluca Baio, James Kirkbride, Christina Ding A modelling framework for estimation of benefit using single arm clinical trials Gianluca Baio, Anthony Hatswell, Nick Freemantle No matching items",
